    "result": "I implemented `order_total` in `solution.py` following the seven rules in `spec.md`, keeping the given signature and the `CouponError` class. Validation runs first, then the subtotal, coupon checks (expiry is inclusive, used codes, minimum subtotal, kind), the percent or fixed discount (fixed is capped at the subtotal), shipping on the discounted subtotal (10.00 below 100.00, free otherwise, none for an empty order), and a final `ROUND_HALF_UP` to cents. I wrote `tests/test_solution.py` with 29 pytest cases covering each rule and its boundaries. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes with 29 passed. One test expectation was my own error at first: a 100% coupon leaves a discounted subtotal of 0, which is below 100.00, so shipping of 10.00 applies. I corrected the test to match the spec. Two choices I made where the spec is silent: I reject `bool` quantities as non-integers, and a coupon with an unrecognised kind raises `CouponError` before its value is checked.",
